&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Prime Minister.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Prime Minister&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The Prime Minister is the&lt;strong&gt; real executive authority and the Head of the Government.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Article 75&lt;/strong&gt; -&amp;nbsp;The Prime Minister is appointed by the President.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The Prime Minister is the &lt;strong&gt;ex-officio Chairman&lt;/strong&gt; of NITI Aayog, National Integration Council, and Inter-State Council.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The tenure of the&amp;nbsp;Prime Minister&amp;nbsp;is not fixed and he holds office during the pleasure of the President for&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;5&amp;nbsp;years.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The oath&amp;nbsp;of office to the&amp;nbsp;Prime Minister&amp;nbsp;is administered by the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;President.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The first and longest-serving&amp;nbsp;Prime Minister of India - &lt;strong&gt;Jawaharlal Nehru.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The current Prime Minister of India&amp;nbsp;- &lt;strong&gt;Narendra Modi.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The oldest Prime Minister&amp;nbsp;of India&amp;nbsp;- &lt;strong&gt;Moraji Desai.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The youngest Prime Minister&amp;nbsp;of India&amp;nbsp;- &lt;strong&gt;Rajiv Gandhi.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Speaker of the Lok Sabha&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;The Speaker&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;is the&amp;nbsp;Presiding Officer of&amp;nbsp;Lok Sabha.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The Speaker of Lok Sabha is &lt;strong&gt;elected by the members of the Lok Sabha&lt;/strong&gt; from amongst themselves.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The Speaker presides over the &lt;strong&gt;joint sitting (Article 108)&lt;/strong&gt; of both houses of the Parliament.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The Speaker gives his &lt;strong&gt;resignation letter to the Deputy Speaker.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The current Speaker of&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Lok Sabha - &lt;strong&gt;Om Birla.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The first Speaker of&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Lok Sabha - &lt;strong&gt;G. V. Mavlankar.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The first woman Speaker of&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Lok Sabha&amp;nbsp;- &lt;strong&gt;Meira Kumar.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Article 81&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;The Lok Sabha.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The members of the&amp;nbsp;Lok Sabha are&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;directly elected by the people.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The maximum strength of the&amp;nbsp;Lok Sabha&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;fixed at 552&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;(&lt;strong&gt;530&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;are elected members, 20 members from Union Territories.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Lok&amp;nbsp;Sabha is not a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;permanent body and is subject to dissolution&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The tenure of a&amp;nbsp;member&amp;nbsp;of the&amp;nbsp;Legislative Assembly&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;5&amp;nbsp;years.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;money bill (Article 110&lt;/strong&gt;) only can be introduced in&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;Lok Sabha.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Uttar Pradesh&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;has the largest representation in the Lok Sabha&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;(80&amp;nbsp;seats).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Vice-President&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type: disc;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;The Vice-President&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;is the Ex-officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Article 63&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;The&amp;nbsp;Vice-President of India.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The tenure of the Vice-President of India&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;5&amp;nbsp;years.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The oath&amp;nbsp;of office to the&amp;nbsp;Vice-President is administered by the &lt;strong&gt;President.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The Vice-President of India&amp;nbsp;gives his&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;resignation letter to the President.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The current Vice-President of India -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Jagdeep Dhankhar&lt;/strong&gt; (As of September 2022)&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The current Chairman of&amp;nbsp;Rajya Sabha -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Jagdeep Dhankhar&lt;/strong&gt; (As of September 2022)&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The first Chairman of&amp;nbsp;Rajya Sabha -&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Dr. S. Radhakrishnan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The longest-serving Vice-President of India -&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Mohammed Hamid Ansari.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The shortest-serving&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Vice-President of India&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;V. V. Giri.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chairman of the Rajya Sabha​&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type: disc;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;The Vice-President&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;is the Ex-officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The current Deputy Chairman of&amp;nbsp;Rajya Sabha -&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Harivansh Narayan Singh.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The first Chairman of&amp;nbsp;Rajya Sabha -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. S. Radhakrishnan.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The First Deputy Chairman of&amp;nbsp;Rajya Sabha -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;S. V. Krishnamoorthy Rao.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The longest-serving&amp;nbsp;chairman of&amp;nbsp;Rajya Sabha -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Mohammed Hamid Ansari.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The shortest-serving&amp;nbsp;chairman of&amp;nbsp;Rajya Sabha -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;V. V. Giri.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Uttar Pradesh&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;has the largest representation in the Rajya Sabha&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;(31 members).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Rajya Sabha&amp;nbsp;was constituted on&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;April 1952.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Rajya Sabha&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;known as the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Upper House.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Rajya Sabha&amp;nbsp;is a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;permanent body and is not subject to dissolution&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One-third&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of its members&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;retire every two years.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The maximum strength of the Rajya Sabha is fixed at 250 (&lt;strong&gt;238 are elected members and 12 members are nominated by the President&lt;/strong&gt;)&amp;nbsp;having special knowledge or practical experience in the fields of&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;science, literature, arts, and social service.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;At present, there are&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;245 members&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;in the Rajya Sabha. Out of which&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;233 are elected members and 12 are nominated members.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;There is no seat reserved for SCs and STs in Rajya Sabha.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The tenure of a&amp;nbsp;member&amp;nbsp;of the&amp;nbsp;Rajya Sabha&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;6 years.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;members are&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;indirectly elected and nominated&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;by means of a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;single transferable vote&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;fourth schedule&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to the constitution deals with the allocation of seats in the Rajya Sabha to the States and Union Territories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

