&lt;p&gt;TB Solution:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Let the lights be switched off before you leave.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The given sentence is an&lt;strong&gt; imperative sentence&lt;/strong&gt; and in the &lt;strong&gt;present indefinite tense.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In &lt;strong&gt;Present Indefinite&lt;/strong&gt; Tense always have to &lt;strong&gt;use the present form of the main verb&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The rule for changing the present indefinite tense into Active or Passive voice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;diams; Follow the structure&lt;u&gt; &amp;lsquo;Let + subject + be + III&amp;#39; form of the verb.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;diams;&lt;strong&gt;You can also start the Passive with &amp;lsquo;You are ordered/advised/requested (according to the sense of the sentence) + to followed by the complete sentence in the&amp;nbsp;Active Voice. (and it is the easiest way, though informal.&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;diams;.&lt;strong&gt;In case, the sentence starts with &amp;lsquo;Please/Kindly&amp;#39; remove it and start the Passive Voice with &amp;lsquo;You are requested to&amp;#39; followed by the sentence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Speak the truth&lt;/em&gt; (Active voice)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Let the truth be spoken&lt;/em&gt;. (Passive Voice)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corrected sentence:&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Let the lights be switched off before you leave.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;​Hence, &lt;strong&gt;option 4&lt;/strong&gt; is the right answer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words&quot;&gt;First Statement:&lt;strong&gt; &amp;quot;The soldiers loaded their guns and marched towards the battle ground.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; This statement shows that soldiers are preparing for and heading into battle. It tells us what&amp;#39;s happening on the military side.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words&quot;&gt;Second Statement: &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;The families of soldiers are praying for the safety of the soldiers who are in the battle ground.&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; This statement tells us what the soldiers&amp;#39; families are doing while the soldiers are fighting. They are worried about their loved ones and praying for their safety.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words&quot;&gt;Therefore,&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;Statement II is the effect and Statement I is its immediate and principal cause.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hence,&amp;nbsp;the correct answer is &amp;quot;Option 4&amp;quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

