&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is, &lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(88, 89, 91);   &quot;&gt;The lion is a beast of prey&amp;#39;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(88, 89, 91);   &quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;beast of prey&lt;/strong&gt; means any predatory animal, since it doesn&amp;#39;t mention any animal in particular &lt;strong&gt;article &amp;#39;a&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt; is used before beast which has a consonant sound.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lion&lt;/strong&gt; is a singular noun and it represents a whole class, therefore&lt;strong&gt; article &amp;#39;the&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt; is used.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Hence, option 3 is the correct answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, the correct sentence is &lt;em&gt;-&amp;#39;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(88, 89, 91);   &quot;&gt;The lion is a beast of prey&amp;#39;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(88, 89, 91);   &quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;a&amp;#39;, &amp;#39;an&amp;#39;, &amp;#39;the&amp;#39;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;are the three different articles in English.

	&lt;ul style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px;&quot;&gt;
		&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;a&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;is used before a common noun singular with a consonant sound.

		&lt;ul style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px;&quot;&gt;
			&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;a European.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;a university.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;an&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;is used before a common noun singular with a vowel sound.
		&lt;ul style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px;&quot;&gt;
			&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;an umbrella.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;an apple.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;the&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;is used before phrases that specify a person or object.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;the&amp;#39; is used before something unique.
		&lt;ul style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px;&quot;&gt;
			&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;the last day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;the first building.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;the equator.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;the moon.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Serene&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The most appropriate antonym for the highlighted word in the given sentence is &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;serene&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agitated:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;worried or angry
	&lt;ul&gt;
