&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sachchidanand Sinha&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sachchidanand Sinha&lt;/strong&gt; was the oldest member of the Constituent Assembly, hence he was appointed as the temporary president of the first meeting following the French practice.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The first meeting of the Constituent Assembly took place on &lt;strong&gt;December 9, 1946&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;His role as the temporary president was to oversee the election of the permanent president of the Assembly, which led to the election of &lt;strong&gt;Dr. Rajendra Prasad&lt;/strong&gt; on December 11, 1946.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Sachchidanand Sinha&amp;#39;s appointment as the temporary president is a testament to the respect and honor accorded to him by his peers in the Assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

