		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Submission- &lt;/strong&gt;The action of accepting or yielding to a superior force or to the will authority of another person.
		&lt;ul&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example-&lt;/strong&gt; I&amp;#39;m preparing the results of my study for&lt;strong&gt; submission&lt;/strong&gt; to a medical journal.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maniacs- &lt;/strong&gt;A person exhibiting extremely wild or violent behaviour.
		&lt;ul&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example- &lt;/strong&gt;Some &lt;strong&gt;maniacs &lt;/strong&gt;were running down the street waving a massive bar.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;We have to&amp;nbsp;use the most appropriate word for the given blank.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;An expert or teacher always develops the child.So,the hint goes to the word&lt;strong&gt; Development.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Therefore, the most appropriate word for the given blank is&lt;strong&gt; Development.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The complete phrase is:&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt; An expert(the teacher) knows more than they do about their own child&amp;#39;s&lt;u&gt; development.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thus, the correct answer is option no.&lt;strong&gt;(1)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is option no.(2) i.e. &lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;Rather&amp;#39;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Let&amp;#39;s take look at the phrase: Her intention was not to bash parents,&amp;mdash;&amp;mdash;&amp;mdash;(4) she wanted to know how to encourage parents.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Let&amp;#39;s see the options:&lt;/strong&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;or:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;used to connect words,phrases or sentences.
		&lt;ul&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:- &lt;/strong&gt;Maria could write her homework now &lt;strong&gt;or &lt;/strong&gt;take a nap.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;rather: &lt;/strong&gt;used to indicate what you want or prefer to do, have,etc.
		&lt;ul&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:-&lt;/strong&gt; I&amp;#39;d &lt;strong&gt;rather &lt;/strong&gt;handle the problem myself.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;so: &lt;/strong&gt;used as a subordinating conjunction to introduce clauses of result or decision.
		&lt;ul&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:-&lt;/strong&gt; It was a long journey, &lt;strong&gt;so&lt;/strong&gt; I&amp;#39;m really tired now.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;yet:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;used to emphasis that we expect something to happen soon.
		&lt;ul&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:- &lt;/strong&gt;Have you finished your homework&lt;strong&gt; yet&lt;/strong&gt;?&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;We can see the explanation of the options.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The phrase has a slight contradiction or we choose one between bash parents or&amp;nbsp;she wanted to know how to encourage parents.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;So, the use of rather will give an appropriate meaning for the given blank.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The complete phrase is: &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Her intention was not bash parents,&lt;u&gt;rather&lt;/u&gt; she wanted to know how to encourage parents.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is option &lt;strong&gt;(2).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is option no.(3) i.e.&lt;strong&gt; &amp;#39;Judgement&amp;#39;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

